@title Tides of Trade: Press Release
@subtitle Brightwater Maritime Museum, press room

# At a glance
kpi Opens | 2026-11-14 | closes 2027-05-09
kpi Objects | 140 | from 12 countries

The exhibition "Tides of Trade" opens to the public on 2026-11-14 and closes on 2027-05-09. It brings together 140 objects from 12 countries and is curated by Dr. Rasmus Lindholm.

# About the exhibition
"Tides of Trade" follows the spice, tea and cotton routes between 1600 and 1850. It draws on original ship ledgers and navigation instruments, and includes a full-size reconstruction of a cargo hold. The centerpiece is the 1783 log of the brig Hesper, shown publicly for the first time.

# Visiting
- Adults: $18
- Seniors: $14
- Children under 12 and museum members: free
- Open Tuesday to Sunday, 10:00 to 17:00, and until 20:00 on Thursdays
- The exhibition is fully step-free

# Programs
- Opening gala on 2026-11-13 at 18:30, tickets $120
- Curator talk every first Saturday at 14:00
- Free school visits for groups of up to 40 students, booked at schools@brightwatermuseum.example

